### Aiming on Node.js 4

This release drops Node.js 0.10/0.12 support, so we replaced lots of modules and reduce dependency tree more than twice ([see PR overview](https://github.com/sindresorhus/got/pull/140)). Module folder size reduced from `1.1 MB` to `216 KB`.

For older Node.js versions we will still maintain [`v5.x`](https://github.com/sindresorhus/got/tree/v5.x) for critical bug-fixes.

### Promises by default

Callback interface was replaced by Promises, because it is a better way to work with asynchronous operations and they can be used with `yield`/`await` nicely.

If you use callback before:

``` js
got('todomvc.com', (err, body) => {
    if (err) {
        console.log(err);
        return;
    }

    console.log(body);
});
```

You can rewrite it this way:

``` js
got('todomvc.com')
    .then(res => {
        console.log(res.body);
    })
    .catch(err => {
        console.log(err);
    });
```

You can read more about Promises in ["ECMAScript 6 promises (2/2): the API"](http://www.2ality.com/2014/10/es6-promises-api.html) post and some caveats in ["We have a problem with promises"](http://pouchdb.com/2015/05/18/we-have-a-problem-with-promises.html).

### Update

```
$ npm install --save got@6
```

### Changes

https://github.com/sindresorhus/got/compare/v5.3.0...v6.0.0

- 54bd6f5bbad9590be6ffc7baf004c381bf1ea7a9 default intervals between delays decreased - now they are around 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, etc...
- a10a99e8ae6cfb84522795605ce0014877fb9f52 `retries` option accepts backoff function, for example you can:

``` js
// Constant delay of 10ms for 5 iterations
got('google.com', {
    retries: iter => iter < 5 && 10
});

// Infinity retries with constant delay
got('google.com', {
    retries: () => 10
});
```

